 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A 3D grid of voxels. For each voxel, a scalar field value $V$ is computed. The scalar field is generated by accumulating contributions from metaballs (blobs) and a floor term for each voxel [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Output:** A stream of triangles (positions and normals) rendered immediately to the GPU.
+*   **Input:** A 3D grid of voxels. Field generation computes the 3D scalar field by accumulating contributions from all metaballs and a floor term for each voxel [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Output:** A stream of triangles (positions and normals) rendered immediately to the GPU [S1, unofficial].
 
